## Original Content
The support will benefit children in three Sudanese states; West Darfur, South Kordofan and Gedaref with the aim of restoring “safe, quality and inclusive education” amid the world's largest humanitarian and displacement crisis.

## Summary
The UN has launched a $22m initiative to restore safe, quality, and inclusive education for children in three Sudanese states amid a major humanitarian crisis. The states benefiting are West Darfur, South Kordofan, and Gedaref. This effort aims to address the educational needs of children affected by the world's largest displacement crisis.

## Key Points
- $22m UN initiative for education in Sudan
- Targets West Darfur, South Kordofan, and Gedaref
- Aims for safe, quality, and inclusive education amid humanitarian crisis


